//! Safe Rust bindings for the Kylin vector-engine-client SDK
//! (`libkysdk-vector-engine-client`).
//!
//! Uses [`libloading`] to load `libkysdk-vector-engine-client.so` at runtime
//! so the workspace still builds and runs on hosts without the SDK installed.
//! Type definitions are generated by bindgen when the `stub` feature is not
//! enabled and the SDK headers are available.
//!
//! # Library search order
//!
//! 1. `KART_VECTOR_DB_SDK_PATH` environment variable (full path to .so)
//! 2. System library path matching the build target architecture
//!    (`/usr/lib/<debian-triple>/libkysdk-vector-engine-client.so`)
//! 3. Next to the running binary (deployment scenario)
//! 4. Bare SONAME — defers to the dynamic linker (ldconfig / `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`)
//!
//! # Stub feature
//!
//! Enable the `stub` Cargo feature to compile without the SDK or `libclang`.
//! All public API surface still exists, but every call returns
//! [`KylinVectorDBError::LibraryNotFound`].
//!
//! # Safety
//!
//! This crate is the only place where `unsafe` is permitted for the
//! vector-engine-client SDK. All `unsafe` is confined to `extern "C"` call
//! sites; the public API is fully safe Rust.

